CM_ BU_ PD16A "Haltech Nexus PD16 power distribution module, box A (base CAN ID 0x6D0). Other boxes shift the base: B=0x6D8, C=0x6E0, D=0x6E8 and inputs to 0x321/0x325/0x329 etc.";
CM_ BU_ KEYPAD "Haltech 15-button (3x5) CAN keypad, CANopen node ID 12. ECU also polls node IDs 10, 11 and 13 (0x60A/0x60B/0x60D) for keypads that are not fitted; those IDs are left undecoded.";
CM_ BO_ 800 "PD16 A AVI 1-4 switch state and pin voltage, 100Hz. Haltech Multiplexed CAN Protocol v2.0.";
CM_ BO_ 804 "PD16 A SPI 1-4 switch state and pin voltage, 100Hz.";
CM_ BO_ 808 "PD16 A SPI 1-4 measured input frequency, 100Hz.";
CM_ BO_ 1744 "ECU -> PD16 A output duty/frequency commands, 20Hz base rate. Mux byte = IO type (bits 7-5) | IO index (bits 3-0): type 0 = 25A HCO, 1 = 8A HCO, 2 = half bridge.";
CM_ BO_ 1745 "ECU -> PD16 A output and input pin configuration, 2Hz. Mux types: 0 = 25A HCO, 1 = 8A HCO, 2 = half bridge, 3 = SPI, 4 = AVI.";
CM_ BO_ 1746 "ECU -> PD16 A system configuration, 2Hz. Not observed on this bus yet.";
CM_ BO_ 1747 "PD16 A input state/voltage/duty/frequency, 20Hz base rate. Mux types: 3 = SPI, 4 = AVI (PD16 has no DPI or button inputs).";
CM_ BO_ 1748 "PD16 A output load/voltage/current and fault state, 5Hz base rate. Mux types: 0 = 25A HCO, 1 = 8A HCO, 2 = half bridge. On 8A muxes 1-4 bytes 7 carries the matching 25A HCO retry count / pin state.";
CM_ BO_ 1749 "PD16 A device status and firmware version, 2Hz.";
CM_ BO_ 1750 "PD16 A rail voltages, temperatures, total current and serial, 2Hz. Plain mux 0-5 in byte 0.";
CM_ BO_ 396 "CANopen TPDO1 from the 15-button (3x5) keypad, node ID 12. Sent on button change. Byte 0 bits 0-7 = buttons 1-8, byte 1 bits 0-6 = buttons 9-15 (1 = pressed).";
CM_ BO_ 1804 "CANopen heartbeat from keypad node 12, every 150ms.";
CM_ BO_ 1548 "CANopen SDO download request ECU -> keypad node 12. Observed writing object 0x6200 (digital outputs = button LEDs).";
CM_ BO_ 1420 "CANopen SDO response keypad node 12 -> ECU.";
